        "original_id": "a5a0d9e6-2c8c-566f-904f-042f6c1f66d6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikael Åkerfeldt, Lee Ranaldo, Thurston Moore, Steven Wilson\n- Bands/Projects: Opeth, Bloodbath, Steel, Storm Corrosion, Sonic Youth\n- Publications/Lists: Rolling Stone, Spin, Greatest Guitarists of All Time\n- Songs/Albums: Youth Against Fascism, Dirty\n\nFacts:\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was born on 17 April 1974 and is a Swedish musician.\n- Lee Ranaldo was born on February 3, 1956 and is an American musician, singer-songwriter, guitarist, writer, visual artist, and record producer.\n- Sonic Youth released the album Dirty in 1992.\n- \"Youth Against Fascism\" was the second single from Sonic Youth's 1992 album Dirty.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is the lead vocalist, guitarist, and primary songwriter of Opeth.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was the former vocalist of Bloodbath.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was also guitarist for the one-off band Steel.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is part of the collaboration Storm Corrosion with Steven Wilson.\n- Lee Ranaldo is best known as a co-founder of Sonic Youth.\n- In 2004, Rolling Stone ranked Lee Ranaldo number 33 on its Greatest Guitarists of All Time list.\n- In May 2012, Spin published a staff-selected top 100 ranking that placed Thurston Moore and his Sonic Youth bandmate Lee Ranaldo together at number 1.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
